{"description":"Enforce per-role guardrails: the mandatory worker sandbox (env allow-list reusing `pluginEnv`, process-group spawn hardening, checksum trust per ADR-028) and per-worker git-worktree isolation, plus a default-deny permission policy for ACP `session/request_permission`. Guardrails are code-owned and non-optional in v1.","acceptanceCriteria":"Workers run with the allow-listed env only; no host env inheritance.\nEach worker gets its own git worktree.\nACP permission requests are default-denied unless explicitly allowed and never hang.\nThe sandbox is enabled by default with no opt-out in v1."}